# NOTE: `*.spec.ts-snapshots/` USED TO BE IGNORED HERE, and the reasoning is
# worth keeping because it names what had to be true before it could be
# un-ignored: nothing under it was a reviewed reference, the spec wrote a
# baseline on first run and passed against itself, and committing whichever
# branch ran last would have promoted that branch's rendering to the
# reference. Two things were required — baselines generated on the platform
# CI renders on, and a decision about which commit is "correct".
#
# Both are now settled, so the directory is TRACKED:
#   * the baselines were generated on a GitHub ubuntu-latest runner (the
#     files are suffixed -chromium-linux; PNGs from a laptop or an agent
#     sandbox rasterise fonts differently and will fail in CI), and
#   * the reference is `main` — they were produced on a branch whose diff
#     against main is workflow-only, so the rendering is main's.
#
# Un-ignoring them is what lets `layout-vrt.spec.ts` be a gate rather than
# smoke coverage. Regenerate deliberately, never to "make CI green": see the
# spec's docblock for the exact command.

# Audit run output — regenerated by `frontend-audit.spec.ts` on every run.
# The findings that matter live in docs/TNM-MENU-01/FRONTEND-AUDIT.md;
# committing the raw per-route JSON would churn on every environment.
e2e/audit-report/
